+# FlameAtlas Research Platform — The Flamels
+
+The dedicated The Flamels edition of SpaceFire-AI. The complete scientific application and NASA source files are retained, with FlameAtlas branding, an original flame mark, a navy/mint interface, isolated browser preferences, a provenance page and links to The Flamels evidence presentation and GitHub repository.
+
+Upstream implementation: [COngtuthien/SpaceFire-AI](https://github.com/COngtuthien/SpaceFire-AI), pinned to `9817452c3effdf03864dea65f23d1f767b33251b`. Read `UPSTREAM_README.md` for the original credits and methodology. No upstream license file was provided; no new license is asserted over that material.
+
+## Run this edition from The Flamels repository
+
+```bat
+git clone https://github.com/tun539/the-flamels.git
+cd the-flamels
+setup.cmd
+launch.cmd
+```
+
+The Flamels launcher clones the complete pinned source into its ignored runtime folder, verifies source-file hashes, applies the reviewed edition patch, installs dependencies, builds the database and builds the frontend. It leaves the existing FlameAtlas MVP source intact.
+
+For a materialized checkout of this edition on Linux, use `scripts/setup.sh` followed by `scripts/start.sh --prod`. On Windows use the included `setup.cmd` and `launch.cmd`.
+
+## Included application
+
+- Research-to-Safety Explorer and a guided presentation journey.
+- Combustion Explorer, investigation and record details, compatible comparison and condition similarity.
+- Five conceptual 3D studios: droplet flame extinction, solid flame spread, spacecraft fire, gaseous flames and smoke detection.
+- Scientific charts, source documents and NASA media with provenance.
+- Cited Research Copilot, literature discovery, knowledge graph and data reliability tools.
+- An exploratory FLEX estimator, kept separate from measured results and accompanied by its upstream validation limitations.
+- Light/dark/system themes and responsive navigation.
+
+The Copilot works in evidence-only mode without a provider key. Configure your own key only in the materialized checkout's gitignored `.env` to enable model-written answers. No model key is included or copied from upstream.
+
+The extended application has its own schema and catalogue. Its record counts are not added to the original FlameAtlas summary counts. Imported curated derivatives preserve their upstream source status; inclusion does not imply independent re-verification by The Flamels.
+
+Local execution and a private Codespace are supported. The existing public presentation remains available separately; publishing it does not host this application's FastAPI backend.
+
+Research support tool. Not a certified fire safety assessment. NASA does not endorse this project.
